  "bank.h": "Banking apps (pause Accessibility, USB debugging)", "bank.p": "Some apps (banks, wallets, carriers, a few games) won't open while any accessibility service or USB debugging is on. Pick any app on the kid's phone, or type the package name of one not installed yet. When the kid opens an app on this list, KidGuard turns its Accessibility and Developer options / USB debugging off (the kid is told), then puts back exactly what was on 1 minute (basic mode) or 10 minutes (Device Owner) after they leave it. Meanwhile the screen and adb can't be used; time limits and app blocks still work.", "bank.n": { one: "{0} app listed · tap to choose", other: "{0} apps listed · tap to choose" }, "bank.find": "Find an app", "bank.pkg": "Package name, e.g. com.VCB", "bank.add": "Add", "bank.bad": "Not a valid package name (like com.name.app)", "bank.notInst": "not installed",
